-- #1383 face 1.  `Holder`'s sole variant is the NAMED-FIELD CONSTRUCTOR `Plain`, so
-- this declaration is filed in the record registry under key `Plain` while a value of
-- it has head tycon `Holder`.  That gap is what sends `mkH.hx` down the field→owners
-- fallback: `lookupRecordByName "Holder"` misses and no key suffix-matches `__Holder`.
--
-- Its two fields are ordered OPPOSITELY to plainlib's, so picking the other `Plain`
-- is observable as a VALUE and not only as a diagnostic.  (The single-field corpus is
-- what let #1382 ship: both layouts pick index 0 and a wrong pick is invisible.)
public export data Holder =
  | Plain { hx : Int, hy : Int }

export mkH : Holder
mkH = Plain { hx = 100, hy = 200 }
